course: dictionary
lesson: 10425
title: Trolling: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one is meant. «Trolling means sending many cruel messages online; you can disagree strongly with someone without abusing them.» The clues are online, cruel messages and abusing, so here trolling means being mean online on purpose.
explain: Trolling can also mean fishing: a boat slowly pulls a baited line behind it. It can mean teasing too, as in «I'm just trolling you». Read the whole sentence, then ask which meaning fits best.
explain: Trolling online is a kind of cyberbullying, and it can really hurt people. If someone trolls you, the safe steps are: do not reply, block them, report them and tell an adult you trust.
fact: Trolling means posting rude, mean or upsetting messages online on purpose, to make people angry or to get attention.
fact: Trolling can also mean fishing by pulling a baited line behind a slowly moving boat.
fact: Among friends, trolling can be playful teasing, but it can still hurt.
fact: Trolling online is a kind of cyberbullying.
fact: «Don't feed the trolls» means don't reply to them, because replies give them the attention they want.
exercise: «Trolling means sending many cruel messages online; you can disagree strongly with someone without abusing them.» What does trolling mean in this sentence? | Fishing from a slow boat | Drawing a funny picture | *Sending cruel messages online on purpose | Reading a long book
exercise: A boat moves slowly while a baited line is pulled behind it. What is this called? | *Trolling | Sailing | Swimming | Anchoring
exercise: Max laughs and says, «I'm just trolling you». What does trolling mean here? | *Teasing someone as a joke | Asking for help | Sending cruel messages online | Fishing from a boat
test: Someone posts cruel messages online to upset people on purpose. What is this called? | Gardening | Painting | Reading | *Trolling
test: What is the best thing to do if someone trolls you online? | Share their messages with your friends | *Do not reply, block them, report them and tell an adult | Reply angrily to them | Pretend you did not see it and post cruel messages back
exam: Which sentence uses trolling to mean teasing as a joke? | *"I'm just trolling you," said Sam with a grin | Her messages were trolling, cruel and unkind | The lake was calm, so we went trolling | The fisherman went trolling at dawn on the lake
